From 26cfa2b371ff412c55a5db6b34d7dad76db9ec1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:49:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 52/54] hw/display/pvg: depth clamp / line fill pipeline
 variants, separate vertex-stage bindings, vertex-only pipelines, atomics and
 SIMD-group ops

- SetDepthClipMode / SetTriangleFillMode select pipeline variants
  (depthClampEnable, polygonMode LINE).
- Vertex-stage textures/samplers/constant samplers bind at +64, so both
  stages can use the same Metal index with different resources.
- Pipelines without a fragment function (depth/stencil-only) are built
  with a single stage instead of failing silently.
- air2spv: air.atomic.{global,local}.* -> OpAtomic* (device via physical
  storage buffer pointers, threadgroup via word arrays); air.simd_* /
  air.quad_* -> GroupNonUniform reductions, scans, shuffles, ballot, vote,
  elect; int64 atomics features enabled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
